check 1
# A walk in the Rogue Encampment from one shared input script: ScnAma,
# -seed 1234; before frame 10's drain a left click at (600, 300) (client
# pixels, 800 x 600), on 1.14d posted to the window at the tick-return stop
# of frame 9, on d2rs sent through the bridge's world-click dispatcher
# after the snapshot of frame 9. Compare the player's mode, path target and
# position frame by frame. Spec: specs/tools/scenario-diff.md §2 rule 4.
name walk-town-ama
save ScnAma --class ama --expansion
seed 1234
ticks 80
seconds 240
channels state packets
input frame 10; click 600 300
# Every field compared (rc-walk-town: equal on integ-r16 without the old
# `ignore seed s fc sp`); packets compared too, so the C->S of the click
# is checked against the d2rs client gap (scenario-diff.md open question 6).
